NAME
       tr - translate, squeeze or delete characters

SYNOPSIS
       tr [-d] [-s] set1 [set2]

DESCRIPTION
       Reads standard input, transforms it and writes standard output.
       By default each character of SET1 is replaced by the character
       at the same position in SET2.

       Sets accept ranges such as a-z and the classes [:upper:]
       [:lower:] [:digit:] [:space:] [:alpha:] [:alnum:].

OPTIONS
       -d     delete every character in SET1
       -s     squeeze repeats of the characters in the last set

EXAMPLES
       tr a-z A-Z < notes.txt
       tr -d '\r' < dos.txt > unix.txt
       tr -s ' '

SEE ALSO
       sed(1), cut(1)
